  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through Thursday)\nIssued at 244 PM CDT Fri Sep 25 2026\n\nUpper ridging continues to build back over west Texas and SE NM \nSunday, ahead of another storm system. Highs Sunday and Monday look \nto reach the 80s (western counties) to 90s. Monday, our next storm \nsystem begins to approach our area. Lift along the edge of the \ntrough brings the return of rain chances to our western zones during \nthe afternoon, spreading eastward through the evening and overnight \nhours. Long-range models suggest moisture from Hurricane Polo \nbecomes entrained into the upper trough as it swings over New Mexico \nTuesday. As the system and its associated cold front translates over \nour region Tuesday into Wednesday, rain chances increase areawide. \nSomething to monitor next week is the potential for heavy rainfall \nleading to flash flooding, especially if moisture from Polo combines \nwith the trough. There remains a lot of uncertainty regarding the\nexact setup and specific impacts with this upcoming system. \nOtherwise, lowering heights Tuesday result in highs ranging in the\n80s to low 90s. A cold front brings widespread highs in the 80s, \nwith 70s in the higher terrain Wednesday and Thursday afternoons.",
